														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4044305">
									

<p>I can't quite lay my finger on it, but some bits don't read like an SCP report.<br />
Like some claiming the space to be theoretically infinite, it's something I feel wouldn't be mentioned or phrased another way.</p>
<p>Second, sharing of flesh and crops containing flesh.<br />
Are they Sarkic?<br />
I mean they are formed from &quot;His&quot; flesh, which brings me doubt, but flesh crops is very reminiscent of sarkics.</p>
<p>That said, I don't dislike this.<br />
It's whole, complete and explained.<br />
The voice logs are nicely done, I however don't feel a journal entry would be made into a voice log. I feel like first contact would be added in a report, not just the passing by of a researcher and a farmer.</p>
<p>In any case, this is a nicely written first SCP.<br />
+1</p>

